    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-29T21:17:38+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-29T21:17:38+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T11:47:38Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-29T11:47:38Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A series of slow moving troughs will move over the west of SA on Tuesday then will across remaining parts of the state on Wednesday and Thursday as a couple of cold fronts move across waters to the south. A high pressure system will become established south of the Bight during Friday and persist there on Saturday. A trough will extend from WA over the far west of SA over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-29T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds in the far west. Winds southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers in the far west, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Coober Pedy. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 35.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 3:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. A thunderstorm likely, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Light winds becoming northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 31.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, most likely in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy. Winds southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
